      "status": "approve",
      "reasoning": "The complete TOGO M1344 provider record explicitly lists Fe2(SO4)3・nH2O, 0.02g in main solution1, separately from its copper stock and trace stock. Its original JCM1250 route returns Nothing found, now correctly classified as unsuccessful rather than positive primary evidence. The frozen formula and provider interpretation support balanced variable hydration, with no selection of n. The unchanged composed payload retains the prior B aliases and local primary with asymmetric CHEBI53438 parent, rejects malformed Fe(SO4)3, and does not substitute monohydrate CHEBI131387. All inherited full-owner, quantity and downstream release holds remain.",
